# Project Structure

Purpose: canonical layout for `frontend/`.

## Root structure

```txt
frontend/
├── .cursor/
├── .github/workflows/
├── dev-plan/
├── analysis_options.yaml
├── l10n.yaml
├── pubspec.yaml
├── README.md
├── assets/
│   ├── icons/
│   ├── images/
│   ├── illustrations/
│   └── logos/
├── docs/
├── env/
├── lib/
├── test/
├── integration_test/
└── tool/
```

`dev-plan/` and `.cursor/` are planning/rules only — not imported by app code.

## `lib/` structure

```txt
lib/
├── main.dart
├── bootstrap.dart
├── app/
│   ├── app.dart
│   ├── locale/
│   ├── router/
│   ├── startup/
│   └── theme/
├── core/
│   ├── config/
│   ├── errors/
│   ├── logging/
│   ├── network/
│   ├── permissions/
│   ├── responsive/
│   ├── security/
│   ├── storage/
│   ├── sync/
│   └── utils/
├── features/<feature_name>/
│   ├── data/
│   ├── domain/
│   └── presentation/
├── l10n/
└── shared/
    ├── components/
    ├── data/
    ├── forms/
    ├── layout/
    ├── search/
    └── widgets/
```

## Rules

- `features/<feature_name>` for product behavior and screens.
- `core` for cross-cutting infrastructure used by multiple features.
- `shared` for reusable UI, layouts, forms, and search helpers not tied to one feature.
- No feature-specific business logic in `core` or `shared`.
- No duplicate folders/files for the same responsibility.
- Tests mirror source structure.

